{
  "version": 1,
  "source_hash": 5077417410359805164,
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Fibonacci Numbers",
      "source_hash": 11323574609811877564,
      "context_hash": 3759670541747396923,
      "translation": "피보나치 수",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562471Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The Fibonacci sequence is defined as follows:",
      "source_hash": 7820455405699789664,
      "context_hash": 9097896009010097697,
      "translation": "피보나치 수열은 다음과 같이 정의됩니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562472Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "The first elements of the sequence ([OEIS A000045](http://oeis.org/A000045)) are:",
      "source_hash": 17109563246798170129,
      "context_hash": 4248672826238501214,
      "translation": "이 수열의 처음 몇 항([OEIS A000045](http://oeis.org/A000045))은 다음과 같습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562472Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Properties",
      "source_hash": 7934823041470838436,
      "context_hash": 16191627098575474702,
      "translation": "성질",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562472Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Fibonacci numbers possess a lot of interesting properties.",
      "source_hash": 2214219072925354602,
      "context_hash": 17707602570925592103,
      "translation": "피보나치 수에는 흥미로운 성질이 많습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562472Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "Here are a few of them:",
      "source_hash": 5505046537050564560,
      "context_hash": 12468406603235610097,
      "translation": "그중 몇 가지는 다음과 같습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562472Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Cassini's identity:",
      "source_hash": 71231385442262268,
      "context_hash": 13966162831657816280,
      "translation": "카시니 항등식:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562472Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "This can be proved by induction.",
      "source_hash": 2602529596835329279,
      "context_hash": 2097044441637673941,
      "translation": "이는 귀납법으로 증명할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562472Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:4/seg:1",
      "source": "A one-line proof by Knuth comes from taking the determinant of the 2x2 matrix form below.",
      "source_hash": 2381841241850476107,
      "context_hash": 7084241872749027995,
      "translation": "Knuth의 한 줄짜리 증명은 아래의 2x2 행렬 형태에서 행렬식을 취하여 얻어집니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562473Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "The \"addition\" rule:",
      "source_hash": 4965602119840673955,
      "context_hash": 9672962434010597481,
      "translation": "\"덧셈\" 규칙:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562473Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:7/seg:0",
      "source": "Applying the previous identity to the case $k = n$, we get:",
      "source_hash": 17899570619660412554,
      "context_hash": 10716581608594896849,
      "translation": "앞의 항등식을 $k = n$인 경우에 적용하면 다음을 얻습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562473Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:9/seg:0",
      "source": "From this we can prove by induction that for any positive integer $k$,  $F_{nk}$ is multiple of $F_n$.",
      "source_hash": 1310152913231822216,
      "context_hash": 12513215847453112336,
      "translation": "이로부터 임의의 양의 정수 $k$에 대하여 $F_{nk}$가 $F_n$의 배수임을 귀납법으로 증명할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562473Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:10/seg:0",
      "source": "For $n \\ge 3$, the inverse is also true: if $F_m$ is multiple of $F_n$, then $m$ is multiple of $n$.",
      "source_hash": 14158734097166069481,
      "context_hash": 18226065867841249677,
      "translation": "$n \\ge 3$일 때는 그 역도 성립합니다: $F_m$이 $F_n$의 배수이면 $m$은 $n$의 배수입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562473Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:11/seg:0",
      "source": "GCD identity:",
      "source_hash": 15748669334100106255,
      "context_hash": 11978025773570043266,
      "translation": "GCD 항등식:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562473Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:13/seg:0",
      "source": "Fibonacci numbers are the worst possible inputs for Euclidean algorithm (see Lame's theorem in [Euclidean algorithm](euclid-algorithm.md))",
      "source_hash": 8480798465779564249,
      "context_hash": 16766594343087809557,
      "translation": "피보나치 수는 유클리드 알고리즘에 대해 가능한 최악의 입력입니다([유클리드 알고리즘](euclid-algorithm.md)의 라메 정리를 참고하십시오)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Fibonacci Coding",
      "source_hash": 8353039946289429378,
      "context_hash": 3434452358071833702,
      "translation": "피보나치 부호화",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "We can use the sequence to encode positive integers into binary code words.",
      "source_hash": 6159708790461612523,
      "context_hash": 4477828079526595062,
      "translation": "이 수열을 사용하여 양의 정수를 이진 부호어로 부호화할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "According to Zeckendorf's theorem, any natural number $n$ can be uniquely represented as a sum of Fibonacci numbers:",
      "source_hash": 16950335270886774705,
      "context_hash": 4657070125784645779,
      "translation": "제켄도르프 정리에 따르면, 모든 자연수 $n$은 피보나치 수의 합으로 유일하게 표현될 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "such that $k_1 \\ge k_2 + 2,\\ k_2 \\ge k_3 + 2,\\  \\ldots,\\  k_r \\ge 2$ (i.e.: the representation cannot use two consecutive Fibonacci numbers).",
      "source_hash": 10630795311241174701,
      "context_hash": 6254388609459502433,
      "translation": "이때 $k_1 \\ge k_2 + 2,\\ k_2 \\ge k_3 + 2,\\  \\ldots,\\  k_r \\ge 2$를 만족합니다(즉, 이 표현에서는 연속된 두 피보나치 수를 사용할 수 없습니다).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "It follows that any number can be uniquely encoded in the Fibonacci coding.",
      "source_hash": 11068709614313446368,
      "context_hash": 13973310714354838105,
      "translation": "따라서 모든 수는 피보나치 부호화로 유일하게 부호화될 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:4/seg:1",
      "source": "And we can describe this representation with binary codes $d_0 d_1 d_2 \\dots d_s 1$, where $d_i$ is $1$ if $F_{i+2}$ is used in the representation.",
      "source_hash": 1705390066453902790,
      "context_hash": 4265315401425432298,
      "translation": "그리고 이 표현을 이진 부호 $d_0 d_1 d_2 \\dots d_s 1$로 나타낼 수 있으며, 여기서 $d_i$는 표현에 $F_{i+2}$가 사용되면 $1$입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:4/seg:2",
      "source": "The code will be appended by a $1$ to indicate the end of the code word.",
      "source_hash": 9955798962520967888,
      "context_hash": 14938708090226128051,
      "translation": "부호어의 끝을 나타내기 위해 부호 뒤에 $1$을 덧붙입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:4/seg:3",
      "source": "Notice that this is the only occurrence where two consecutive 1-bits appear.",
      "source_hash": 11441661732557617063,
      "context_hash": 9296088495760320775,
      "translation": "연속된 두 개의 1비트가 나타나는 곳은 이곳뿐이라는 점에 유의하십시오.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "The encoding of an integer $n$ can be done with a simple greedy algorithm:",
      "source_hash": 13872004434696315166,
      "context_hash": 8671449789485991729,
      "translation": "정수 $n$의 부호화는 간단한 탐욕 알고리즘으로 수행할 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:7/seg:0",
      "source": "Iterate through the Fibonacci numbers from the largest to the smallest until you find one less than or equal to $n$.",
      "source_hash": 10723760167361733149,
      "context_hash": 17542951426999989493,
      "translation": "$n$ 이하인 수를 찾을 때까지 피보나치 수를 가장 큰 것부터 가장 작은 것 순으로 순회합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:8/seg:0",
      "source": "Suppose this number was $F_i$.",
      "source_hash": 15942592290811560027,
      "context_hash": 1918030200671463822,
      "translation": "이 수가 $F_i$였다고 합시다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562474Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:8/seg:1",
      "source": "Subtract $F_i$ from $n$ and put a $1$ in the $i-2$ position of the code word (indexing from 0 from the leftmost to the rightmost bit).",
      "source_hash": 5877110112061749798,
      "context_hash": 18233524439221951230,
      "translation": "$n$에서 $F_i$를 빼고 부호어의 $i-2$ 위치에 $1$을 놓습니다(가장 왼쪽 비트부터 가장 오른쪽 비트까지 0부터 인덱싱합니다).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562475Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:9/seg:0",
      "source": "Repeat until there is no remainder.",
      "source_hash": 6641356915383838803,
      "context_hash": 11332448077629562413,
      "translation": "나머지가 없을 때까지 반복합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562475Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:10/seg:0",
      "source": "Add a final $1$ to the codeword to indicate its end.",
      "source_hash": 17709032527423361670,
      "context_hash": 8410478298300125072,
      "translation": "부호어의 끝을 나타내기 위해 마지막에 $1$을 덧붙입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562475Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:11/seg:0",
      "source": "To decode a code word, first remove the final $1$.",
      "source_hash": 13940788064500336916,
      "context_hash": 15042395867296554157,
      "translation": "부호어를 복호화하려면 먼저 마지막 $1$을 제거합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562475Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:11/seg:1",
      "source": "Then, if the $i$-th bit is set (indexing from 0 from the leftmost to the rightmost bit), sum $F_{i+2}$ to the number.",
      "source_hash": 12065224796190534579,
      "context_hash": 13621019650701201107,
      "translation": "그다음 $i$번째 비트가 설정되어 있으면(가장 왼쪽 비트부터 가장 오른쪽 비트까지 0부터 인덱싱합니다) 수에 $F_{i+2}$를 더합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562475Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Formulas for the $n^{\\text{th}}$ Fibonacci number",
      "source_hash": 16422006255916370050,
      "context_hash": 15430139206453259220,
      "translation": "$n^{\\text{th}}$ 피보나치 수에 대한 공식",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.562475Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Formulas for the <script type='math/tex'>n</script>-th Fibonacci number",
      "source_hash": 16993811980763697422,
      "context_hash": 8493966040668844266,
      "translation": "<script type='math/tex'>n</script>번째 피보나치 수를 구하는 공식",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563247Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Closed-form expression",
      "source_hash": 6164831582148106742,
      "context_hash": 8421835937403005274,
      "translation": "닫힌 형태의 식",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563247Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "There is a formula known as \"Binet's formula\", even though it was already known by Moivre:",
      "source_hash": 7316110483858240018,
      "context_hash": 1394959080298479002,
      "translation": "Moivre가 이미 알고 있었지만 \"Binet의 공식\"으로 알려진 공식이 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563247Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "This formula is easy to prove by induction, but it can be deduced with the help of the concept of generating functions or by solving a functional equation.",
      "source_hash": 4885192805671113714,
      "context_hash": 7782337918712385881,
      "translation": "이 공식은 귀납법으로 쉽게 증명할 수 있습니다. 또한 생성 함수의 개념을 이용하거나 함수 방정식을 풀어서 유도할 수도 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563247Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:6/seg:0",
      "source": "You can immediately notice that the second term's absolute value is always less than $1$, and it also decreases very rapidly (exponentially).",
      "source_hash": 6297257021519095464,
      "context_hash": 11502720079538956056,
      "translation": "두 번째 항의 절댓값은 항상 $1$보다 작고 매우 빠르게(지수적으로) 줄어든다는 것을 바로 알 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563247Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:6/seg:1",
      "source": "Hence the value of the first term alone is \"almost\" $F_n$.",
      "source_hash": 13527180689726664673,
      "context_hash": 12045657977171961534,
      "translation": "따라서 첫 번째 항의 값만으로도 \"거의\" $F_n$입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:6/seg:2",
      "source": "This can be written strictly as:",
      "source_hash": 3415091026656104748,
      "context_hash": 2105685238878563152,
      "translation": "이는 엄밀하게 다음과 같이 쓸 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:8/seg:0",
      "source": "where the square brackets denote rounding to the nearest integer.",
      "source_hash": 1504639166528599740,
      "context_hash": 10930881261199337963,
      "translation": "여기서 대괄호는 가장 가까운 정수로 반올림한다는 뜻입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:9/seg:0",
      "source": "As these two formulas would require very high accuracy when working with fractional numbers, they are of little use in practical calculations.",
      "source_hash": 16406866329361530218,
      "context_hash": 16870009322776413285,
      "translation": "이 두 공식은 소수를 다룰 때 매우 높은 정밀도가 필요하므로 실제 계산에서는 거의 쓸모가 없습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:10/seg:0",
      "source": "Fibonacci in linear time",
      "source_hash": 7433429413117774640,
      "context_hash": 15937650044761456643,
      "translation": "선형 시간에 피보나치 수 구하기",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:11/seg:0",
      "source": "The $n$-th Fibonacci number can be easily found in $O(n)$ by computing the numbers one by one up to $n$.",
      "source_hash": 7667342880770623442,
      "context_hash": 61036083775457781,
      "translation": "$n$번째 피보나치 수는 $n$까지 수를 하나씩 계산하여 $O(n)$에 쉽게 구할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:11/seg:1",
      "source": "However, there are also faster ways, as we will see.",
      "source_hash": 9541802444087016670,
      "context_hash": 9591543779793677256,
      "translation": "하지만 뒤에서 살펴보듯이 더 빠른 방법도 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:12/seg:0",
      "source": "We can start from an iterative approach using the formula $F_n = F_{n-1} + F_{n-2}$.",
      "source_hash": 15472175556626817578,
      "context_hash": 11411582437798025452,
      "translation": "$F_n = F_{n-1} + F_{n-2}$ 공식을 이용하는 반복적 접근법에서 시작할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:12/seg:1",
      "source": "The implementation only needs to keep the two most recent values, starting from the base cases $F_0$ and $F_1$.",
      "source_hash": 2827371225994398212,
      "context_hash": 13847412188843316517,
      "translation": "구현할 때는 기저 사례인 $F_0$과 $F_1$에서 시작하여 가장 최근의 두 값만 저장하면 됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:14/seg:0",
      "source": "In this way, we obtain a linear solution with $O(n)$ time and $O(1)$ additional memory.",
      "source_hash": 6251220471398892623,
      "context_hash": 6466516479495340534,
      "translation": "이렇게 하면 $O(n)$ 시간과 $O(1)$ 추가 메모리를 사용하는 선형 해법을 얻습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:15/seg:0",
      "source": "Matrix form",
      "source_hash": 3769887857381719359,
      "context_hash": 6652742258549336265,
      "translation": "행렬 형태",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:16/seg:0",
      "source": "To go from $(F_n, F_{n-1})$ to $(F_{n+1}, F_n)$, we can express the linear recurrence as a 2x2 matrix multiplication:",
      "source_hash": 12564458368096675411,
      "context_hash": 16601564727992717469,
      "translation": "$(F_n, F_{n-1})$에서 $(F_{n+1}, F_n)$으로 넘어가기 위해 선형 점화식을 2x2 행렬 곱셈으로 나타낼 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:18/seg:0",
      "source": "This lets us treat iterating the recurrence as repeated matrix multiplication, which has nice properties.",
      "source_hash": 16591139145220780895,
      "context_hash": 9172653718839122965,
      "translation": "이렇게 하면 점화식을 반복하는 과정을 행렬 곱셈의 반복으로 다룰 수 있으며, 행렬 곱셈의 반복에는 유용한 성질이 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:18/seg:1",
      "source": "In particular,",
      "source_hash": 7241674802618167537,
      "context_hash": 4733802741386471541,
      "translation": "특히,",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563248Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:20/seg:0",
      "source": "where $F_1 = 1, F_0 = 0$.",
      "source_hash": 15760632354774141219,
      "context_hash": 3413538260847080103,
      "translation": "여기서 $F_1 = 1, F_0 = 0$입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:20/seg:1",
      "source": "In fact, since",
      "source_hash": 4956507220897911495,
      "context_hash": 14190720909576873030,
      "translation": "실제로 다음이 성립하므로",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:22/seg:0",
      "source": "we can use the matrix directly:",
      "source_hash": 13839105907907119713,
      "context_hash": 6983667873699773723,
      "translation": "행렬을 직접 사용할 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:24/seg:0",
      "source": "Thus, in order to find $F_n$ in $O(\\log  n)$ time, we must raise the matrix to n. (See [Binary exponentiation](binary-exp.md))",
      "source_hash": 8262238583755470867,
      "context_hash": 1411406296857956443,
      "translation": "따라서 $F_n$을 $O(\\log  n)$ 시간에 구하려면 행렬을 n제곱해야 합니다. ([이진 거듭제곱](binary-exp.md) 참조)",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:26/seg:0",
      "source": "Fast Doubling Method",
      "source_hash": 461470976287616150,
      "context_hash": 5630350045031609310,
      "translation": "빠른 더블링 방법",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:27/seg:0",
      "source": "By expanding the above matrix expression for $n = 2\\cdot k$",
      "source_hash": 6732218017297199571,
      "context_hash": 13278687029332947917,
      "translation": "위의 행렬 식을 $n = 2\\cdot k$에 대해 전개하면",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:29/seg:0",
      "source": "we can find these simpler equations:",
      "source_hash": 2940987349724846253,
      "context_hash": 3968010556401709562,
      "translation": "다음과 같은 더 간단한 식을 얻을 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:31/seg:0",
      "source": "Thus using above two equations Fibonacci numbers can be calculated easily by the following code:",
      "source_hash": 10689699722151346859,
      "context_hash": 2978535415045822838,
      "translation": "따라서 위의 두 식을 이용하면 다음 코드로 피보나치 수를 쉽게 계산할 수 있습니다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:33/seg:0",
      "source": "The above code returns $F_n$ and $F_{n+1}$ as a pair.",
      "source_hash": 3102884137160969878,
      "context_hash": 3749453929887277200,
      "translation": "위 코드는 $F_n$과 $F_{n+1}$을 쌍으로 반환합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Periodicity modulo p",
      "source_hash": 10442001201702076517,
      "context_hash": 15306419499205468315,
      "translation": "p를 법으로 하는 주기성",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Consider the Fibonacci sequence modulo $p$.",
      "source_hash": 15500104313248988060,
      "context_hash": 8489876353392709108,
      "translation": "$p$를 법으로 하는 피보나치 수열을 생각해 봅시다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:1",
      "source": "We will prove the sequence is periodic.",
      "source_hash": 3679712877569360042,
      "context_hash": 11207889561478120052,
      "translation": "이 수열이 주기적임을 증명하겠습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563249Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "Let us prove this by contradiction.",
      "source_hash": 12805131987938485602,
      "context_hash": 7822255198874542200,
      "translation": "이를 귀류법으로 증명해 봅시다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:2/seg:1",
      "source": "Consider the first $p^2 + 1$ pairs of Fibonacci numbers taken modulo $p$:",
      "source_hash": 15857425132180825209,
      "context_hash": 148476286205673333,
      "translation": "$p$로 나눈 나머지를 취한 피보나치 수의 처음 $p^2 + 1$개 쌍을 생각해 봅시다:",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "There can only be $p$ different remainders modulo $p$, and at most $p^2$ different pairs of remainders, so there are at least two identical pairs among them.",
      "source_hash": 7545155551756572012,
      "context_hash": 13579264315321530428,
      "translation": "$p$로 나눈 나머지는 $p$가지뿐이고 나머지 쌍은 많아야 $p^2$가지이므로, 이들 가운데 똑같은 쌍이 적어도 두 개 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:4/seg:1",
      "source": "This is sufficient to prove the sequence is periodic, as a Fibonacci number is only determined by its two predecessors.",
      "source_hash": 10763457084479457396,
      "context_hash": 1916652995859991096,
      "translation": "피보나치 수는 바로 앞의 두 수만으로 결정되므로, 이것만으로도 수열이 주기적임을 충분히 증명할 수 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:4/seg:2",
      "source": "Hence if two pairs of consecutive numbers repeat, that would also mean the numbers after the pair will repeat in the same fashion.",
      "source_hash": 17662934007577011663,
      "context_hash": 15544838209586330801,
      "translation": "따라서 연속한 두 수의 쌍이 반복된다면, 그 쌍 뒤에 오는 수들도 같은 방식으로 반복된다는 뜻입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "We now choose two pairs of identical remainders with the smallest indices in the sequence.",
      "source_hash": 9456186592911785665,
      "context_hash": 6431541166418494927,
      "translation": "이제 수열에서 인덱스가 가장 작은, 나머지가 같은 두 쌍을 고릅니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:5/seg:1",
      "source": "Let the pairs be $(F_a,\\ F_{a + 1})$ and $(F_b,\\ F_{b + 1})$.",
      "source_hash": 15449717437641588058,
      "context_hash": 18066225786582759514,
      "translation": "이 두 쌍을 $(F_a,\\ F_{a + 1})$와 $(F_b,\\ F_{b + 1})$이라고 합시다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:5/seg:2",
      "source": "We will prove that $a = 0$.",
      "source_hash": 1811330851910168535,
      "context_hash": 17657876469339229731,
      "translation": "$a = 0$임을 증명하겠습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:5/seg:3",
      "source": "If this was false, there would be two previous pairs $(F_{a-1},\\ F_a)$ and $(F_{b-1},\\ F_b)$, which, by the property of Fibonacci numbers, would also be equal.",
      "source_hash": 5105927862587445980,
      "context_hash": 10131033065904126839,
      "translation": "이것이 거짓이라면 바로 앞의 두 쌍 $(F_{a-1},\\ F_a)$와 $(F_{b-1},\\ F_b)$가 존재하며, 피보나치 수의 성질에 따라 이 두 쌍도 같아야 합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:5/seg:4",
      "source": "However, this contradicts the fact that we had chosen pairs with the smallest indices, completing our proof that there is no pre-period (i.e the numbers are periodic starting from $F_0$).",
      "source_hash": 15370153919239741924,
      "context_hash": 10298388502091947360,
      "translation": "그러나 이는 인덱스가 가장 작은 쌍을 골랐다는 사실에 모순되므로, 전주기가 없다는 것(즉, 수열은 $F_0$부터 주기적이라는 것)이 증명됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-09-24T11:03:50.563645Z",
      "issues": []
    },
